          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-05 20:53:43.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19582 tests: avoid statfs cache in recovery-small 147",
        "message": "LU-19582 tests: avoid statfs cache in recovery-small 147\n\nTest 147 evicts the client and relies on \"lfs df\" to send an RPC to\nOST0000 and so start the reconnect with lost connect replies. The\nclient serves statfs from its cache for OBD_STATFS_CACHE_SECONDS\n(1s), so when another statfs had just run, \"lfs df\" sent nothing,\nthe evicted client never reconnected, the idle import was\ndisconnected and the test failed with \"Client reconnected too slow\".\n\nSleep past the cache lifetime before \"lfs df\" so the RPC is always\nsent.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=recovery-small env=ONLY=147\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5d6ffe181f78078f105ea109fb69800ad48af2b2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
